Subject: [ZEROX 09/09] High-density backpressure and adaptive async execution

Targets:
- CraftAsyncScheduler
- CraftScheduler / ZeroxSchedulerGuard
- RegisteredListener
- ZeroxJoinLoadController
- GlobalConfiguration
- ZeroxBootstrap and build metadata

Behavior:
- replaces CallerRunsPolicy so saturated async plugin work is never executed on the submitting/main thread;
- preserves overflow work in an off-main queue with explicit backpressure;
- adapts async concurrency from main-thread MSPT and measured synchronous plugin work;
- reserves CPU capacity for the authoritative tick thread;
- pauses, but does not discard, progressive join chunk expansion under pressure;
- reduces per-player chunk send/load/generation bursts for high-density deployments;
- retains synchronous Bukkit event ordering, cancellation and world mutation semantics;
- records that 200-300 players on 8 GiB requires production workload validation and is not guaranteed.

Default density values:
- target MSPT: 20
- reserve main cores: 2
- async overflow queue: 16384
- player chunk send/load/generate rates: 24/36/8 per second
- concurrent player chunk loads/generates: 3/1
- maximum joins finalized per tick: 1

No task, event, chunk request or explosion is dropped by this patch.
